  "id": "bimanual-coordination",
  "term": "bimanual coordination",
  "definition": "Bimanual coordination is the ability to organize the movements of both arms or hands in relation to each other, including patterns of relative timing or phase between them. In learning research, it refers to practicing and improving these linked two-limb movement patterns under different kinds of feedback.",
